{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Kronecker","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.binding_juxtapose_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.binding_juxtapose_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L197-L205","doc":"**Binding of a juxtaposed pair vanishes.** If the assembly is a genuine disjoint union (no\nlinking), the mass-deficit binding is zero — the components are independent. Binding is therefore\ncarried entirely by the FAILURE of juxtaposition, i.e. by the linking, which is what\n`bindingFreeEnergy` measures. This is the falsifiable content of the whole bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_juxtapose_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_juxtapose_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L181-L194","doc":"**Adding a `1×1` identity BLOCK costs no free energy** — at the matrix level.\n\n🛑 The physical gloss that stood here (\"a disjoint trivial component contributes nothing to the\nmass, as it must\") is FALSE and is retracted (bean `qou-bsfg`). A braid closure on `n` strands is\nnormalised by `δ^{n−1}`, so juxtaposition drops exactly one loop factor: the cost is `log δ =\n0.6985808249` at `q₀`, and `⁴He` is short by `≈ 2.096`. Machine-checked in\n`QOU.Mass.ClosureNormalisationDefect` (`freeEnergy_closureNorm_additive_iff`: additivity holds iff\n`δ = 1`, which `loopValue_ne_one` excludes for `q > 1`). This lemma is retained as the matrix-level\nfact it is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_juxtapose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_juxtapose","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L170-L178","doc":"**The archimedean bridge on juxtaposed amplitudes — multiplicativity DISCHARGED.** For two\ncomponents whose composite evaluation is their disjoint-strand juxtaposition, the observable free\nenergy is additive. The multiplicativity is not assumed: it is `markovTrace_juxtapose`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.binding_eq_qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.binding_eq_qInt","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L140-L152","doc":"**The binding identity with the positivity hypothesis DISCHARGED**, for amplitudes drawn from\nthe quantum-integer class (constituent self-amplitudes `Tᵢ = [nᵢ]_q`, interaction factor `[m]_q`).\nNo `0 < T` is assumed: at the substrate `q > 1` positivity is a theorem (`qIntR_pos`). The\nmass-deficit binding equals the connected free energy `−log [m]_q`. Only the *multiplicativity* input\n— that the assembly amplitude factorises as `(∏ Tᵢ)·[m]_q` — remains carried by the shape of the\nstatement; that is the Jones-connected-sum theorem, the open formalisation item. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.qIntRProd_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.qIntRProd_pos","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L135-L138","doc":"A finite product of quantum integers at `q > 1` is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.qIntR_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.qIntR_pos","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L126-L133","doc":"**A quantum integer at `q > 1` is strictly positive** — a sum of positive powers. This is the\npositivity the framework's amplitudes carry (quantum dimensions are built from `[n]_q`), so `0 < T`\nis discharged by the substrate constraint `q > 1`, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.qIntR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.qIntR","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L121-L124","doc":"The quantum integer `[n]_q = ∑_{i<n} qⁱ`, restated inline to keep this file Mathlib-only (the\ncanonical form is `QOU.MathlibExt.qInt`, `= ∑ i ∈ range n, q^i`; `qInt_pos` there proves the same\npositivity). The Mass files in this arc are deliberately self-contained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.bindingFreeEnergy_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.bindingFreeEnergy_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L99-L106","doc":"**A bound state has positive binding iff its interaction factor is below one.** With the\nmass-deficit sign convention, `bindingFreeEnergy I > 0 ↔ I < 1`: the assembly amplitude is\n*suppressed* relative to independent constituents exactly when the state is bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.bindingFreeEnergy_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.bindingFreeEnergy_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L85-L97","doc":"**Binding vanishes exactly at independence.** For a positive interaction factor, the binding\nfree energy is zero iff the assembly amplitude factorises (`I = 1`, no interaction). Binding is\npurely the connected part — the free-energy form of `binding_indep_of_self`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.binding_eq_bindingFreeEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.binding_eq_bindingFreeEnergy","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L73-L83","doc":"**The self/mutual partition, lifted to the multiplicative trace.** If the assembly amplitude is\n`(∏ Tᵢ) · I` (constituent self-traces times the interaction factor), the observable free energy\nsplits as `Σ Eᵢ + log I`, so the mass-deficit binding `Σ Eᵢ − E_assembly` equals `−log I =\nbindingFreeEnergy I`. This is `SelfMutualPartition.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy` DERIVED at the\nMarkov-trace level: the additivity is a consequence of trace multiplicativity, not an assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.bindingFreeEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.bindingFreeEnergy","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L69-L71","doc":"The interaction (connected) free energy of an assembly whose amplitude is the product of the\nconstituent self-amplitudes times an interaction factor `I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_prod","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L62-L67","doc":"Extensivity over many constituents: the free energy of a product of positive self-amplitudes is\nthe sum of the constituent free energies. Rest mass adds over the `A` nucleons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_connectedSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_connectedSum","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L52-L60","doc":"**Multiplicative trace ⟹ additive free energy.** The Markov/Jones trace is multiplicative under\nconnected sum (`J(K₁#K₂) = J(K₁)·J(K₂)`); its archimedean image `E = log T` is therefore additive.\nThis is why rest mass is EXTENSIVE (adds over constituents) — the additive-energy model of\n`SelfMutualPartition` is the log-image of the multiplicative self-trace, not an independent\nassumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ArchimedeanTraceBridge.lean#L48-L50","doc":"The archimedean functor on a positive categorical amplitude `T`: the observable free energy\n`E = log T`. (Sign convention: `log`; the mass-deficit binding is `−` the interaction free energy.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}